The files under vendor/ are derived from that project:

  vendor/contracts.ts       DeepSeek web route table and constants
  vendor/request-codec.ts   Request encoders for the DeepSeek web routes
  vendor/stream-codec.ts    SSE stream parser for the DeepSeek web protocol
  vendor/pow.ts             DeepSeekHashV1 proof-of-work solver
  vendor/errors.ts          Error types used by the above
  vendor/types.ts           Shared SSE event type
  vendor/sha3_wasm_bg.wasm  DeepSeek's published proof-of-work WebAssembly module

Modifications made in this project, relative to the upstream sources:

  1. Import specifiers carry explicit .ts extensions so Node's native
     TypeScript type stripping can resolve them without a build step.
  2. vendor/stream-codec.ts imports the SSE event type from a local
     vendor/types.ts instead of the upstream application-wide module, so the
     vendored set has no dependency on the original project layout.
  3. vendor/pow.ts loads its WebAssembly module from disk beside the file
     rather than through chrome.runtime.getURL, which does not exist outside a
     browser extension.

No protocol logic was changed. Request encoding, route matching, stream
parsing, fragment classification, and the proof-of-work algorithm are byte-for-
byte the upstream implementations.

